        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Shame of a City, Unchained Memories, Tigre Hill\n- People: Tigre Hill\n- Events: Philadelphia Film Festival\n- Organizations: Federal Writers' Project, WPA Slave Narrative Collection\n\nFacts:\n- Unchained Memories is a 2003 documentary film about stories of former slaves who were interviewed during the 1930s as part of the Federal Writers' Project and preserved in the WPA Slave Narrative Collection.\n- The Shame of a City is a 2006 feature-length documentary that premiered at the Philadelphia Film Festival.\n- Tigre Hill is perhaps best known for his first documentary, The Shame of a City.",
